  "instructions": [
    "Combine the diced tomato with the fresh basil, dried oregano, a pinch of salt, 1 to 1⅓ tablespoons of the olive oil, and a splash (1 teaspoon) of balsamic vinegar. Chill.",
    "Slice the baguette into ¼ to ½-inch slices. Cut off the end of the garlic clove and rub the garlic onto each side of each piece of bread. Drizzle both sides of the sliced bread with a little olive oil (or use a brush to brush it on).",
    "Toast on a grill or in a hot skillet until browned on both sides.",
    "Top the hot bread with the cold tomato bruschetta and serve immediately."
